@@ -92,3 +92,9 @@ Stop and record an open defect when the same failure fingerprint repeats twice,
 ## Agent budget
 
 Do not create an Agent merely because a workflow stage exists. The planner requests independent roles only at closure candidate, completion, high-risk, actual UI interaction/design work, or explicit human-review triggers. Plain user-visible text does not imply UI/UX work. Keep one leased writer; independent roles are read-only and receive only the contract summary, affected requirements/files, exact gate input, and the artifact they must return.
+
+### External Python governance tools
+
+The command schema (version 1) accepts an optional per-command `trusted_external_entrypoint` object with exactly two string fields: `path` (the canonical absolute regular Python script file) and `sha256` (its current lowercase 64-character SHA-256). Existing project-local commands omit it; the public template stays project-local by default. For an external tool, resolve its actual installed entry, hash its bytes, put that exact absolute path in `argv`, and record the complete shell-quoted command in a project-local normative declaration used by `source`, `source_selector`, and `source_command`. Do not use an environment-variable placeholder in the final manifest. The validator CLI remains `flowctl.py check commands MANIFEST --project-root .`; trust comes from the hashed manifest, not a CLI bypass.
+
+The binding permits only that Python script entry, including normal Python flags before the script. Missing/unknown fields, unused bindings, noncanonical paths, symbolic-link aliases, missing files, and hash drift fail closed. The gate planner also reads and hashes the live external entry, so changing it invalidates command evidence. Source files and working directories remain project-relative; this execution declaration never expands module ownership or project write scope. The hash binds entry bytes, not all imported dependencies or OS-level isolation; bind required dependency/configuration fingerprints separately in the existing context contract. Reinstallation changes the path/hash: refresh the declaration and rerun affected gates instead of reusing stale receipts.
